## Components

- Default to server-side rendering for content/SEO-driven apps; use client-side rendering for SPAs, widgets, or offline-first apps. Match the app type.
- Push client-side boundaries to leaf components — never on wrappers/layouts.
- Composition over configuration. Pass children/slots, not boolean toggle props.

## Data Fetching

- Never use local state + side effects for data fetching (e.g., useState+useEffect, reactive state+onMounted). Use server-side data loading or a dedicated query library.
- Fetch data in parallel in sibling components — avoid request waterfalls.
- Never roll custom in-memory cache in serverless. Use framework caching primitives.

## Server-Side Mutations

- Server-side mutation endpoints are public HTTP endpoints — always re-verify auth/authz inside each handler.
- Defense-in-depth auth: request interceptor (optimization only) → mutation handler (verify authentication) → data access layer (verify authorization). Never rely on interceptors as sole auth check.
- After mutation, invalidate affected caches/paths per framework API.
- Return error unions from mutation handlers, don't throw to the client.

## Accessibility

- Native HTML elements first. Only ARIA when no semantic element exists.
- Every interactive element must be keyboard accessible.
- Every image needs alt text. Decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Manage focus after navigation, modal open/close, and dynamic content changes.

## Performance

- Core Web Vitals targets: LCP < 2.5s, INP < 200ms, CLS < 0.1.
- Virtualize lists/tables exceeding 100 rows.
- Use framework image component with width/height. Prefer modern formats (WebP/AVIF).
- Prioritize LCP resource loading. Lazy-load below-fold images.